# Eye~Helpi Desktop Agent

The machine-side half of Eye~Helpi: a local Ollama brain with an **agentic
tool-calling loop** and a tool registry the phone, the CLI and any MCP client
can all drive.

## Runs on macOS, Linux and Windows

The agent detects the OS automatically and picks the right machinery per tool:
- **Battery**: pmset (Mac) / `/sys/class/power_supply` (Linux) / PowerShell CIM (Windows)
- **Screen capture**: screencapture (Mac) / gnome-screenshot, scrot or ImageMagick (Linux) / PowerShell System.Drawing (Windows)
- **Camera & recording**: ffmpeg on all three (avfoundation / video4linux2+x11grab / dshow+gdigrab)
- **Reminders & Calendar**: macOS today; other OSes report gracefully
- **Weather, network diagnostics, file search, disposal**: pure stdlib — identical everywhere

Install Ollama on the host machine (any OS), then:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt        # standard library only, nothing to install
ollama pull llama3.2-vision            # the vision brain
python main.py chat                    # interactive chat with tool calling
python main.py serve --port 8765       # HTTP API for the phone / scripts
```

