## What's inside

- `main.py` - chat REPL + HTTP API. The chat loop asks the model, executes any
  tool calls it requests, feeds results back, up to 6 rounds per question.
- `tools/__init__.py` - the tool registry: name -> function + description +
  JSON schema, in Ollama tool format.
- `tools/device_controls.py` - macOS device control: battery, screen capture,
  webcam frame, media encoding, background recordings with user-approved
  disposal of anything older than an hour.
- `tools/productivity_tools.py` - Reminders, Calendar, weather (wttr.in),
  network diagnostics, file search.
- `tools/mcp_server.py` - Model Context Protocol server over stdio, exposing
  every registered tool to any MCP client:

  ```json
  {"command": "python", "args": ["-m", "tools.mcp_server"], "cwd": "<agent folder>"}
  ```

## Phone setup

In the iOS app's Setup tab, point the agent host at this Mac's LAN address
(e.g. `http://192.168.1.20:11434`). The phone talks to Ollama directly for
streaming chat; `python main.py serve` exposes the tool API when you want the
phone to trigger desktop device control.